IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc19-s492-21-to-24.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART XV.1 Unreasonable Delay (text lines 10957-10973):
-- s 492.21 (definitions "court" and "unreasonable delay"), s 492.22 (jurisdiction not lost), s 492.23 (stay of proceedings only in
-- accordance with this Part) and s 492.24 (common law rules and principles).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws
-- Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Imports the keel's core only. Every answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE    the text, in its own words, says yes to the case;
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, a flat negative, an "if", "where" or "except" that is not met);
--   NOTHING      not covered: the text is silent, limits itself in its own wording, leaves the case to a judgment or a source outside this text.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every JUST FALSE branch carries `FALSE-kind` and every NOTHING branch `NOTHING-kind`.
-- The functions named for a bar answer JUST TRUE for "barred"; JUST FALSE for a bar means only "this section does not bar it", and is not a grant.

§ `PART XV.1 Unreasonable Delay -- Definitions (s 492.21)`

-- The lead-in says where the two definitions apply: "in this Part". Part XV.1 is sections 492.21 to 492.31 (the next heading, PART XVI, begins at line 11032).
-- A provision outside the Part is not covered (a scope limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)). Section numbers are decimals, so 492.3 sorts between 492.29 and 492.31.
-- src:10961 | 492.21 The following definitions apply in this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.21 (src:10961)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision`'s `section` AT LEAST 492.21 AND `the provision`'s `section` AT MOST 492.31
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in this Part"

-- "court" in this Part is a court seized of an application for a determination of unreasonable delay. A "means" definition, so a body that is not
-- such a court is outside it (JUST FALSE).
-- src:10962 | court means a court seized of an application for a determination of unreasonable delay. (tribunal)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.21 "court" (src:10962)
GIVEN `the body is a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is seized of an application for a determination of unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.21 court` MEANS
    IF `the body is a court` AND `the court is seized of an application for a determination of unreasonable delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a court seized of an application for a determination of unreasonable delay"

-- "unreasonable delay" is a delay that exceeds the reasonable time, for a person charged with an offence to be tried, in accordance with paragraph 11(b) of
-- the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms. The Charter is not among the sources, so what the Charter says is the INPUT (the Charter's answer):
-- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING where it is not known. A NOTHING from the Charter is carried through, never turned into FALSE.
-- src:10963 | unreasonable delay means a delay that exceeds the reasonable time for a person charged with an offence to be tried in accordance with paragraph 11(b) of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms. (délai déraisonnable)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.21 "unreasonable delay" (src:10963)
GIVEN `the delay exceeds the reasonable time for a person charged with an offence to be tried in accordance with paragraph 11(b) of the Charter, by the Charter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.21 unreasonable delay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the delay exceeds the reasonable time for a person charged with an offence to be tried in accordance with paragraph 11(b) of the Charter, by the Charter`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in accordance with paragraph 11(b) of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms"
    WHEN JUST exceeds THEN
        IF exceeds
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a delay that exceeds the reasonable time for a person charged with an offence to be tried"

§ `Jurisdiction (s 492.22)`

-- The finding does not take away the jurisdiction of a court seized with the proceedings over the offence, the accused or the offender. A flat negative (N2: it counts as the
-- text's no), so the answer to "does the finding deprive the court of jurisdiction?" is JUST FALSE for the three things the text names (fork F1). Where no finding has been made, or the
-- court asked about is not seized with those proceedings, or the thing asked about is none of the three, the section does not speak: NOTHING.
-- src:10967 | 492.22 A finding of unreasonable delay by a court in respect of any proceedings does not deprive a court seized with those proceedings of jurisdiction in respect of the offence, the accused or the offender.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.22 (src:10967)
DECLARE `s 492.22 matter of jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.22 the offence`
    `s 492.22 the accused`
    `s 492.22 the offender`
    `s 492.22 anything else`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.22 (src:10967)
GIVEN `a court has made a finding of unreasonable delay in respect of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court asked about is seized with those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 492.22 matter of jurisdiction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.22 a finding of unreasonable delay deprives the court of jurisdiction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a court has made a finding of unreasonable delay in respect of the proceedings`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A finding of unreasonable delay by a court in respect of any proceedings"
        IF NOT (`the court asked about is seized with those proceedings`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a court seized with those proceedings"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 492.22 anything else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of the offence, the accused or the offender"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not deprive a court seized with those proceedings of jurisdiction in respect of the offence, the accused or the offender"

§ `Application: stay of proceedings (s 492.23)`

-- "A court shall not order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay except in accordance with this Part." A bar with an exception.
-- The function is named for the BAR: JUST TRUE = the court is barred; JUST FALSE = this section does not bar it (the "except" is met: the stay is in accordance with this Part), which is not a
-- grant; NOTHING = the stay is not one "as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay", which the section does not speak to.
-- What "in accordance with this Part" requires is the rest of the Part (s 492.31(1) in particular); it is taken as a fact stated by the caller, so that each section answers for itself (fork F2).
-- src:10971 | 492.23 A court shall not order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay except in accordance with this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.23 (src:10971)
GIVEN `the stay of proceedings would be ordered as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stay would be ordered in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.23 the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the stay of proceedings would be ordered as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay"
        IF `the stay would be ordered in accordance with this Part` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in accordance with this Part"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule: the court SHANT order the stay unless it is in accordance with this Part. The text gives no period, so there is no WITHIN.
-- The action carries the one fact the exception turns on, and the guard lets a stay in accordance with this Part pass without breach.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.23 (src:10971)
DECLARE `s 492.23 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.23 order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` HAS `in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Criminal Code s 492.23 (src:10971)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.23 act`
`s 492.23 the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    SHANT `s 492.23 order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` accordance PROVIDED NOT (accordance)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 492.23: a stay of proceedings was ordered as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay otherwise than in accordance with Part XV.1"

§ `Common law rules and principles (s 492.24)`

-- "Rules and principles of the common law in respect of a determination of unreasonable delay continue to apply except insofar as they are altered by or are inconsistent with this Part."
-- The question is asked of one rule or principle, and of the part of it in issue ("insofar as"). JUST TRUE: it continues to apply. JUST FALSE: the part in issue is altered by, or inconsistent
-- with, this Part ("except insofar as"). NOTHING: it is not a common-law rule or principle in respect of a determination of unreasonable delay, which the section does not speak to (fork F3).
-- src:10973 | 492.24 Rules and principles of the common law in respect of a determination of unreasonable delay continue to apply except insofar as they are altered by or are inconsistent with this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.24 (src:10973)
GIVEN `it is a rule or principle of the common law in respect of a determination of unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part in issue is altered by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part in issue is inconsistent with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.24 the rule or principle of the common law continues to apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is a rule or principle of the common law in respect of a determination of unreasonable delay`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rules and principles of the common law in respect of a determination of unreasonable delay"
        IF `the part in issue is altered by this Part` OR `the part in issue is inconsistent with this Part` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except insofar as they are altered by or are inconsistent with this Part"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
